    "updated_at": "2022-01-07T18:00:22Z",
    "body": "I see what you mean. The current approach is trying to maximally reuse definitions, notably \"shadow-including descendants\" and \"shadow-including tree-order\". But doing so means we then have to check the ancestors.\r\n\r\nInstead we could reimplement those definitions (i.e. do our own shadow-including depth-first preorder traversal), and then tweak the result to not traverse into non-delegatesfocus descendants. That might be cleaner indeed.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
